# hessboost vs XGBoost 3.4.1 on an Apple M3 Max (macOS 26.6.2, Rust
# 1.98.1, XGBoost PyPI wheel). Median of six fits per engine, from the
# same run as the tables in docs/performance.md, section 'XGBoost
# comparison'. Threads share dense f32 data, CPU hist, depth 6, 256 bins
# 100 rounds. Chart source for docs/benchmarks/charts.gp.
#
# One row per workload, median fit seconds at 1, 4 and 16 threads
# (hessboost and XGBoost interleaved).
#
# label                seq_t1    xgb_t1    seq_t4    xgb_t4   seq_t16   xgb_t16
"Regression 100k × 30"      0.4584    1.0544    0.2009    0.3665    0.2644    0.3619
"Regression 50k × 128"      1.1534    3.2002    0.4523    0.9943    0.4281    0.6694
"Binary 100k × 30"          0.4589    1.0442    0.1965    0.3656    0.2560    0.3612
"4-class 50k × 30"          1.0938    2.5057    0.5227    0.9807    0.7465    1.2185
